nadoes  flooding hurricanes what have you  all natural disasters as you could think  of them and what we find is that over  over the period of time is uh the rate  of death from  natural disasters and remember world  population has increased four times  since  uh the beginning of the century has has  declined  99 percent and more a major  environmental problem is climate change  left unchecked it is literally an  existential threat to the health of our  planet  and our very survival the world is going  to end in 12 years if we don't address  climate change bailly says these claims  are based on a misreading of u.n  climate change reports there's no cliff  that we're running off of  all it means is well it's going to be  warmer than 1.5 degrees most  likely temperature increases will cause  real problems  but bailly says we're equipped to deal  with them thanks to technology  and economic growth climate change is  going to become a significant problem  but my best guess is that technology  will have the wealth and the technology  for future generations will to be able  to adapt to it and  to start ameliorating what the what  problems that do arise  there will be sea level rise and people  will have to retreat from the coast  but they're not going to have to retreat  tomorrow bailly attributes global  progress to better ideas about how to  organize society  let's sum it up with the word the  enlightenment happen basically the  enlightenment  essentially what happened is democracy  is a way to decide who gets to wield  power  and to be able to throw that out the  second thing is is that we ended up  basically  with uh free markets is that all the  sudden we had property rights and  and there was respect for the rule of  law the the third stool of this  and i think this is the most important  one is called  liberal science how we decide what the  truth is  and it's essentially radical notion of  free speech  is everybody gets to criticize  everybody else and there are n